# Which repo files are NOT uploaded as public static assets.
# Per TDS_Slice_Online_Revamp.md §10, verified by acceptance check §13.10.
#
# `[assets] directory` in wrangler.toml is the repo root, so without this file
# every path below would be downloadable by anyone who knows the URL. Treat it
# as a security boundary, not housekeeping: adding a directory of anything
# non-public to the repo means adding it here in the same commit.
#
# Patterns are relative to the assets directory (the repo root).

.git/
.github/
docs/
fixtures/
node_modules/

# The API's own source. Bundled into the Worker by `main`, never served.
management-app/worker/

# Reaches the Worker as bundled text via the [[rules]] Text glob (§3.7.2), so
# excluding it from *assets* does not stop the in-browser migration runner.
migrations/

# Config and tooling. `wrangler.toml` is not secret — database_id is an
# identifier — but there is no reason to serve it.
wrangler.toml
package.json
package-lock.json

# Every Markdown file at any depth: CLAUDE.md, DEPLOY.md, the SRS/TDS set,
# Interchange_Contract.md, Split_Build_Session_Guide.md.
*.md

# This file itself, and the other repo-root dotfiles.
.assetsignore
.gitignore
